      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Sales Forecasting Dashboard\"\n",
        "description: \"Forecasting 90 days of retail sales using time series decomposition and moving-average models, with interactive Plotly visualisations.\"\n",
        "author: \"Priyadharshini Balaji\"\n",
        "date: \"2026-04-10\"\n",
        "image: \"sales-forecasting.jpg\"\n",
        "categories: [python, time-series, forecasting]\n",
        "format:\n",
        "  html:\n",
        "    code-fold: true\n",
        "    code-tools: true\n",
        "    toc: true\n",
        "execute:\n",
        "  warning: false\n",
        "  message: false\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## The Question\n",
        "\n",
        "*What will our sales look like for the next quarter?* Accurate short-horizon sales forecasts drive staffing, stock, and cash-flow decisions. I build a simple but honest forecast pipeline on two years of synthetic daily sales.\n",
        "\n",
        "## The Approach\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Generate a realistic-looking sales series (trend + weekly seasonality + noise)\n",
        "2. Decompose it into components so we understand *what* is moving\n",
        "3. Forecast the next 90 days with moving-average smoothing\n",
        "4. Build an interactive dashboard to explore the forecast\n",
        "\n",
        "The centred $n$-period moving average used for trend extraction is:[^ma]\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat{T}_t = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=-(n-1)/2}^{(n-1)/2} y_{t+i}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where $y_t$ is the observed sales value at time $t$ and $n = 30$ days is the window chosen to smooth out weekly seasonality without over-smoothing the trend.\n",
        "\n",
        "[^ma]: A centred moving average is preferred over a trailing average for decomposition because it avoids introducing a phase lag into the estimated trend.\n",
        "```{mermaid}\n",
        "flowchart LR\n",
        "    A[Raw Daily Sales] --> B[Decomposition]\n",
        "    B --> C[Trend]\n",
        "    B --> D[Weekly Seasonality]\n",
        "    B --> E[Residual]\n",
        "    C --> F[Forecast Engine]\n",
        "    D --> F\n",
        "    F --> G[90-Day Forecast]\n",
        "    F --> H[80% Confidence Band]\n",
        "    G --> I[Interactive Dashboard]\n",
        "    H --> I\n",
        "    style A fill:#6a4c93,color:#fff\n",
        "    style I fill:#8ac926,color:#fff\n",
        "    style F fill:#ff595e,color:#fff\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "## Step 1 — Simulate daily sales"
      ],
      "id": "91c3917a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: generate-data\n",
        "\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import plotly.graph_objects as go\n",
        "import plotly.express as px\n",
        "from plotly.subplots import make_subplots\n",
        "\n",
        "np.random.seed(7)\n",
        "\n",
        "# 730 days ending today\n",
        "dates = pd.date_range(end='2026-04-15', periods=730)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Trend: slow upward growth\n",
        "trend = np.linspace(1000, 1800, 730)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Weekly seasonality: weekends ~30% higher\n",
        "day_of_week = dates.dayofweek\n",
        "weekly = np.where(day_of_week >= 5, 300, 0) + np.sin(day_of_week * np.pi / 3.5) * 80\n",
        "\n",
        "# Yearly seasonality: December spike\n",
        "month = dates.month\n",
        "yearly = np.where(month == 12, 400, 0) + np.where(month.isin([6, 7]), 150, 0)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Noise\n",
        "noise = np.random.normal(0, 60, 730)\n",
        "\n",
        "sales = (trend + weekly + yearly + noise).round(2)\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame({'Date': dates, 'Sales': sales})\n",
        "df.head()"
      ],
      "id": "generate-data",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 2 — The raw time series"
      ],
      "id": "1c363c90"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-raw-series\n",
        "#| fig-cap: Daily sales over the past 24 months\n",
        "\n",
        "fig = px.line(df, x='Date', y='Sales', template='plotly_white')\n",
        "fig.update_traces(line=dict(color='#6a4c93', width=1.5))\n",
        "fig.update_layout(height=400, title='Daily Sales — 2 year history',\n",
        "                  yaxis_title='Sales (€)', xaxis_title='')\n",
        "fig.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-raw-series",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Straight away you can see **the weekly rhythm** (the fuzzy band), **the trend** (rising baseline), and **the December spike**.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Step 3 — Decompose into trend, season, residual"
      ],
      "id": "f0ea1a29"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-decomposition\n",
        "#| fig-cap: Classical decomposition of the sales series\n",
        "\n",
        "# Simple moving averages to extract components\n",
        "df['Trend'] = df['Sales'].rolling(window=30, center=True).mean()\n",
        "df['Detrended'] = df['Sales'] - df['Trend']\n",
        "df['Seasonal'] = df.groupby(df['Date'].dt.dayofweek)['Detrended'].transform('mean')\n",
        "df['Residual'] = df['Sales'] - df['Trend'] - df['Seasonal']\n",
        "\n",
        "fig = make_subplots(rows=3, cols=1, shared_xaxes=True,\n",
        "                     subplot_titles=('Trend (30-day moving average)', 'Weekly seasonality', 'Residual'))\n",
        "\n",
        "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=df['Date'], y=df['Trend'], line=dict(color='#6a4c93'), name='Trend'), row=1, col=1)\n",
        "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=df['Date'], y=df['Seasonal'], line=dict(color='#1982c4'), name='Season'), row=2, col=1)\n",
        "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=df['Date'], y=df['Residual'], line=dict(color='#ff595e'), name='Residual'), row=3, col=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "fig.update_layout(height=600, showlegend=False, template='plotly_white')\n",
        "fig.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-decomposition",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The decomposition confirms the trend is genuinely increasing (business growing), the weekly seasonality is stable (reliable to forecast), and the residual is well-behaved (no missed pattern).\n",
        "\n",
        "## Step 4 — Forecast the next 90 days"
      ],
      "id": "69d5b16b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-forecast\n",
        "#| fig-cap: Historical sales and 90-day forecast\n",
        "\n",
        "# A simple but honest forecast: trend projection + average seasonality\n",
        "future_dates = pd.date_range(start=df['Date'].max() + pd.Timedelta(days=1), periods=90)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Extend the trend linearly from last known trend value\n",
        "last_trend = df['Trend'].dropna().iloc[-15:].mean()\n",
        "trend_slope = (df['Trend'].dropna().iloc[-15:].mean() - df['Trend'].dropna().iloc[-45:-30].mean()) / 30\n",
        "future_trend = last_trend + trend_slope * np.arange(1, 91)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Apply the weekly seasonality map\n",
        "dow_seasonality = df.groupby(df['Date'].dt.dayofweek)['Seasonal'].mean()\n",
        "future_seasonal = future_dates.to_series().dt.dayofweek.map(dow_seasonality).values\n",
        "\n",
        "forecast = future_trend + future_seasonal\n",
        "\n",
        "# 80% confidence interval from residual std\n",
        "residual_std = df['Residual'].std()\n",
        "upper = forecast + 1.28 * residual_std\n",
        "lower = forecast - 1.28 * residual_std\n",
        "\n",
        "forecast_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    'Date': future_dates,\n",
        "    'Forecast': forecast.round(2),\n",
        "    'Upper': upper.round(2),\n",
        "    'Lower': lower.round(2)\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "fig = go.Figure()\n",
        "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=df['Date'], y=df['Sales'], name='Historical',\n",
        "                          line=dict(color='#6a4c93', width=1)))\n",
        "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=forecast_df['Date'], y=forecast_df['Forecast'], name='Forecast',\n",
        "                          line=dict(color='#ff595e', width=2)))\n",
        "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=forecast_df['Date'], y=forecast_df['Upper'], name='Upper 80%',\n",
        "                          line=dict(color='#ff595e', dash='dot', width=0.5), showlegend=False))\n",
        "fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(x=forecast_df['Date'], y=forecast_df['Lower'], name='80% CI',\n",
        "                          line=dict(color='#ff595e', dash='dot', width=0.5),\n",
        "                          fill='tonexty', fillcolor='rgba(255, 89, 94, 0.15)'))\n",
        "\n",
        "fig.update_layout(height=450, template='plotly_white',\n",
        "                  title='90-Day Sales Forecast with 80% Confidence Band',\n",
        "                  yaxis_title='Sales (€)', xaxis_title='')\n",
        "fig.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-forecast",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 5 — Summary metrics for decision-makers"
      ],
      "id": "08ff0dce"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: summary-metrics\n",
        "\n",
        "total_forecast = forecast_df['Forecast'].sum()\n",
        "avg_daily = forecast_df['Forecast'].mean()\n",
        "peak_day = forecast_df.loc[forecast_df['Forecast'].idxmax(), 'Date']\n",
        "peak_value = forecast_df['Forecast'].max()\n",
        "\n",
        "summary = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    'Metric': ['Total 90-day forecast', 'Average daily sales', 'Peak day', 'Peak value'],\n",
        "    'Value': [f'€{total_forecast:,.0f}',\n",
        "              f'€{avg_daily:,.0f}',\n",
        "              peak_day.strftime('%a %d %b %Y'),\n",
        "              f'€{peak_value:,.0f}']\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "summary"
      ],
      "id": "summary-metrics",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## What this tells the business\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-important title=\"Actionable insights\"}\n",
        "- **Staff up for weekends** — the Saturday/Sunday lift is consistent enough to plan for.\n",
        "- **The forecast trend is upward**, reflecting the underlying growth — capacity planning should reflect that, not flat last-year numbers.\n",
        "- **The 80% confidence band** is tight enough to give stock planners a usable range. Revisit in 30 days with actuals.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## What I learned\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Decomposition before forecasting** is non-negotiable. Looking at trend/season/residual separately showed the pattern was stable and the model could be simple.\n",
        "- **A simple model that you understand** beats a complex one you don't. I could have reached for Prophet or ARIMA, but a moving-average + seasonal map is transparent, cheap to retrain, and adequately accurate for a 90-day horizon.\n",
        "- **Confidence bands matter more than point estimates** — decision-makers need to know the uncertainty, not a pretend-precise single line.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Next steps\n",
